# Best practices

These are the practical rules that make Elastic docs strong and usable.

## General best practices

- Focus on the user goal
- Keep tasks small and specific
- Prefer action-oriented writing
- Keep steps sequential and clear
- Show the outcome when useful
- Link to deeper documentation instead of repeating it

## How-to best practices

- Treat the page like a recipe
- One task per page
- Keep steps independent and easy to follow
- Use clear task titles and prerequisites
- Use success checks when needed

## Overview best practices

- Explain what it is and why it matters
- Cover how it works at a high level
- Avoid expanding into step-by-step instructions
- Link to deeper docs for implementation details

## Tutorial best practices

- Be explicit about audience and learning objectives
- Build from simple to complex
- Include checkpoints after major stages
- Provide realistic examples

## Troubleshooting best practices

- Describe a single problem clearly
- Focus on symptoms first
- Give direct remediation steps
- Order fixes from most common to least common

## Review checklist

Before publishing, ask:
- Does this match the right content type?
- Is the structure complete?
- Are the steps clear and actionable?
- Is the language concise and consistent?
- Is the document accessible and scan-friendly?
- Are the examples realistic and supported?
